  "comment": "grep And the last but not the least, we have the grep command which is a powerful command-line tool in Unix and Linux. It is used for searching and probing data sets for lines that matches a regular expression. As a short history, this utility was coded by Ken Thompson on March 3, 1973 for Unix. Nowadays, Grep is known for detecting and searching for pesky backdoor shells and malicious scripts",
